Embed the pre-built fdlhelper instead of compiling it with cc at runtime.
Drop the HELPER source macro and upstream's foreign_compile(), which
posix_spawn'ed cc. The new foreign_compile() picks the embedded glibc or
musl helper (glibc_helper_data.c, musl_helper_data.c, generated in
postPatch) by which ld.so the host has. It writes the helper to a memfd,
or falls back to /tmp/.musl_dlopen_helper when memfd_create is
unavailable. dlopen, dlsym, dlclose and dlerror become __wrap_*, so
fastfetch's calls reach them through ld --wrap.

